# actions/ — writes only

One file per entity: `actions/projects.ts`. Every `'use server'` mutation lives here.

- Validate with a `validations/` Zod schema before touching Supabase
- Use `ts-pattern` for result/error branching instead of long `if`/`switch` chains
- INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE only — reads belong in `data/`
- `revalidatePath` / `revalidateTag` after successful mutations
- After successful CMS/admin mutations call `recordActivity`; on unexpected server failures call `recordAppError` (see `.cursor/rules/observability.mdc`)
- Never import from `app/`

```ts
'use server'
export async function createProject(input: CreateProjectInput) {
  const parsed = createProjectSchema.parse(input)
  const supabase = await createClient()
  const { error } = await supabase.from('projects').insert(parsed)
  if (error) throw error
  revalidatePath('/projects')
}
```
